      "kind": "note",
      "text": "Prior art (full citations in the linked report): VS Code, Finder, Windows Explorer and GitHub all place the disclosure triangle BEFORE the label and keep it always visible — hover-hiding the ONLY expand affordance measurably hurts discoverability (Nielsen Norman Group; Zach's own Information Scent note). VS Code's own indent-guide default is a faint, low-contrast line, not accent-colored. Block 4 applies all three; blocks 1, 2, 3, 5 and 6 show what changes when you depart from it.",
